      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Scranton’s iconic water tower, erected in 1897, remains the oldest working water tower in Iowa and the ninth oldest in the United States.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scranton%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In February 1907, a fire ignited the water tower when ice melted, yet the tower survived with only minor damage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scranton%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s Marchant Library offers a range of resources, including a historic collection that reflects Scranton’s heritage.",
